# Copy to .env.local for local development. On Vercel, add these under Settings → Environment Variables.

# Eve (the tutor, an eve agent in agent/) and AI grading both reach Claude through Vercel AI Gateway.
# No provider API key is needed anywhere.
# Locally: create a key in the Vercel dashboard → AI Gateway → API keys, and put it here.
# On Vercel: you can leave this unset and let the gateway authenticate with the project's OIDC token
#            (Project Settings → Security → OIDC federation), or set the key here too.
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# Optional. Gateway model id ("provider/model") used for Eve and the grader. Defaults to anthropic/claude-opus-5.
# Any model the gateway lists works, for example anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.
# EVE_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5

# Optional. How hard the grader thinks: low | medium | high. Defaults to medium.
# (Eve's own reasoning effort is set in agent/agent.ts.)
# EVE_EFFORT=medium

# Optional. Neon Postgres connection string. Without it, progress is stored in the browser only.
# Get one at https://neon.tech → your project → Connection string (use the pooled one).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxxx-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
